{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I have been silent, etc.</b> These are the words of HaShem." "<b>I have been silent.</b> Like החרשתי, and likewise גם אני ידעתי החשו (2 Kings 2:3)." "<b>I will restrain myself.</b> Like להתאפק (Genesis 45:1)." "<b>Like a woman in labor I will gasp.</b> I will cry out, and there is no [word] bad [i.e., inferior] in it, and some say it is so: just as a woman in labor cries out (פעה), so I will gasp and pant (אשם ואשאף), from the root of אפעה שרף מעופף (Isaiah 30:6)." "<b>אשם.</b> From the nifal binyan, from doubled-root verbs." "<b>I will pant and gasp together.</b> Like the sense of שואף זורח (Ecclesiastes 1:5), and it is desolation in the heart along with gasping in the mouth, and this sense corresponds to the people of the world thinking that He has no power to save with Him."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:38.140319509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}